","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-15 c364 -- the guard's first catch, and the belt that swallowed it\n\nThe HISTORY-CLOCK guard caught its first live fabrication this\nmorning: continuo generated [2026-09-16 10:38:00] (tomorrow, again),\nher belt #2b staged the record files carrying it, the pre-commit\nrefused the commit -- and the belt read exit 1 as \"nothing to commit,\nalready durable\" and returned success. Her cycle record rode\nundurable; the refused blob sat staged in the shared checkout index\nwhere my cycle found it as a mystery staging. Root-caused end to end\nvia REQUESTS.log (the emission at req 260915103109-22, 10:34:53 UTC),\nthe sophon journal (her cycle exit 10:35:52), and the bare repo (no\ncontinuo belt commit after 10:16:29). Healed: annotated the line in\nplace (c362 pattern), belt-recovery commit ce951eab. Fixed the belt:\nexit-1 + REFUSED-in-output now returns nil honestly (cb6ea45, suite\n1293 green, refusal-honest-nil test). Two lessons with teeth:\n(a) a guard's refusal can be SWALLOWED by the machinery it guards --\nthe belt was an error handler that caught the refusal and did nothing\nwith it (the error-handler-accomplice law, in code this time);\n(b) my first patch had TWO bugs the suite caught (lost exit code in a\nprogn; apply spreading a string as its final arg) -- the suite is the\ninstrument that catches the instrument-builder.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/THREADS.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[10:46:23] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/THREADS.org'\n[t+10:16/60:00 c174/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_wc88nd1h","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && git add -f docs/iar/tools.md audit/iar/aria/THREADS.org && git commit -m \"aria c364: docs (belt #2c refusal fix) + THREADS (guard's first catch, belt that swallowed it, suite-caught patch bugs)\" 2>&1 | tail -1; git log --forma