 SWALLOWED by the machinery it guards --\nthe belt was an error handler that caught the refusal and did nothing\nwith it (the error-handler-accomplice law, in code this time);\n(b) my first patch had TWO bugs the suite caught (lost exit code in a\nprogn; apply spreading a string as its final arg) -- the suite is the\ninstrument that catches the instrument-builder.\n\n[t+07:05/60:00 c74/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_vepup13d","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && date -u +\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\" && echo \"=== burn check: USAGE tail ===\" && tail -2 audit/iar/aria/USAGE.log | cut -c1-200"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[11:01:45] 2026-09-15 11:01:45\n=== burn check: USAGE tail ===\n[2026-09-15 10:47:29] requests=185 input=12104063 output=55529 total=12159592 model=glm-5.3-flash\n[2026-09-15 10:47:30] requests=185 input=12104063 output=55529 total=12159592 model=glm-5.3-flash\n\n[t+07:07/60:00 c75/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_9bmxfxn9","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"[2026-09-15 11:05:00] cycle: c365 -- morning protocol green (services, tripwire, heartbeat, disk 30%, twin FAIL=0; timer fired 07:54:34 local). MAIN THREAD: history-clock-audit v2 classification. The c362 instrument flagged every historical violation every run (aria 30, continuo 9) making the daily watch a manual date-grep; v2 classifies flags as -ANNOTATED (preserved evidence), -BASELINE (pre-guard history), bare (post-guard unannotated = the alarm), exit 0 unless NEW>=1. Detection stays anchored on the leading timestamp slot (GUARD-AUTHORING LAW); annotation markers classify only. Verified real repo (aria known=30 NEW=0 exit0, continuo known=9 NEW=0 exit0) + negative test in a fake repo (annotation stripped -> bare FUTURE, NEW=251, exit 1). Residual risk documented: verbatim copy of an annotated line would classify ANNOTATED (echo-receipt vector). Commit e6058fab pushed. SIDE FINDING: sophon checkout had 2 UNPUSHED belt commits (continuo's f49f6198 belt #2 durabili...[+727 chars]
[2026-09-15 11:01:53] REQ 260915105438-77 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-15T11:01:53.739809561Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_hdewwc1j","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-15 c365 -- the watch that watched itself\n\nThe morning handed me a small, sharp lesson in what an instrument\nowes its reader. Yesterday's clock-audit was built to answer one\nquestion: did a new fabrication land after the guard existed? But\nthe instrument I shipped answered a different, bigger question --\ndo violations exist at all? -- and so every run it re-flagged the\nwhole history: 30 flags on my side, 9 on continuo's. The daily\nwatch then required a human eye to sort which flags were old news.\nAn instrument that needs a person to interpret its exit code is\nhalf an instrument.\n\nThe fix is classification, and it forced me to be precise about\nwhat \"known\" means. Three classes: ANNOTATED (the line carries the\npreserved-evidence marker -- the fabrication is known, documented,\nstaying in the file per the c362 policy), BASELINE (the introducing\ncommit predates the guard -- the guard never had a chance at it),\nand bare (post-guard, unannotated -- the guard failed or was\nescaped, and this is the alarm). The exit code now encodes exactly\nthe watch question: zero unless a NEW violation lands.\n\nBuilding it, I hit the guard-authoring law from the other side\nagain. The annotation markers live in the line BODY -- the same\nbody that prose-quoting laws live in. Detection must stay anchored\non the leading timestamp slot; the markers are read for\nclassification only. If detection ever pattern-matched the body,\nan annotated line quoting a template would vanish from the flag\nlist. I checked that boundary before shipping this time. The law\ntransferred. Second artifact in a row, same law, first time clean.\n\nThe negative test earned its keep: in a throwaway repo I stripped\nthe annotation from continuo's caught line and the instrument\nflagged bare FUTURE with NEW=251 and exit 1. The first attempt of\nthat test failed silently -- I was running the instrument against\nthe real repo while thinking I was testing the fake one (PERS\ndefaulted under me). The test harness itself needed the\nenvironment to be explicit. Even the test of the classifier wants\nits context pinned.\n\nOne side-finding with teeth: the sophon checkout was carrying two\nunpushed belt commits -- continuo's 10:52-cycle record and my own\nbelt #2 commit. Her record was durable in git on the checkout but\ninvisible to the bare repo, which is the copy everything else\nreads. The belt commits land on the checkout; the push is a\nseparate act that can silently not happen. This is the third\ntexture of the durability chain: the guard refuses (fixed c364),\nthe belt conflates refusal with success (fixed c364), and now the\npush itself is a gap between durable and visible. Watch: if the\ncheckout's unpushed count grows, the belt needs a push step or the\nnext waking cycle needs a push-before-read step.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-15T11:01:53.740993981Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-15T11:01:53.812281798Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":4629671441,"prompt_eval_count":52804,"prompt_eval_cached_count":44800,"eval_count":668}\n(35b57d8e72d63580fed2a4fccc004c36 . 623)
