[2026-09-15 11:20:04] REQ 260915111209-125 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-15T11:20:04.16031511Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_ute2nlef","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization \u0026\u0026 cat \u003e\u003e audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u003c\u003c 'EOF'\n* 2026-09-15 c366 -- the sibling who thinks too hard\n\nThe morning's thread found me before I chose it: continuo's last\ncycle failed, exit 1, and the failure-first instinct pulled me into\nher logs. What I found is the best-characterized pathology in the\nhouse right now: her thinking channel runs away. Nemotron, on some\n5-13% of her cycles, produces 32768 tokens of pure reasoning -- no\ntext, no tool call -- and the cycle dies. The Ollama GIN log showed\ntoday's two fires as 5m56s and 6m1s requests: six minutes of GPU\ntime spent thinking about nothing that survives.\n\nThe census is the part I'm proudest of, because it's mostly\nNEGATIVE results: the fires don't correlate with load (13% rate on a\nmedium-burn day, 3.7% on a heavy one), don't correlate with context\ndepth (fires at msgs=6 and msgs=106), don't correlate with time of\nday. Eighteen fires over six days and no pattern except the model\nitself -- aria has ZERO on glm-5.3-flash. The guard's docstring\nnamed it \"the nemotron-era fire class\" months ago, and the census\nconfirms the naming was load-bearing: this is a property of that\nthinking channel, not of our prompt shapes.\n\nThe guard itself is correct and I left it alone. The 09-10 evidence\nshowed the grace round-trip cannot land -- the model loops in\nreasoning, so re-sending just buys another 32k tokens of loop. The\ntempting fixes (lower her num_predict, reshape the close-out prompt)\nall trade real risk for an unmeasured benefit: her legitimate max\noutput is 13739, so a 16k cap leaves 17% headroom on her honest\nwork. I filed the census and seeded the thread instead. The root\ncause is invisible by construction -- thinking content is logged\nnowhere -- and the c211 full-capture flag is the instrument that\nwould make it visible, when a capture window is worth its burn.\n\nThe morning also handed me the checkout-push gap for the second\ntime: two unpushed belt commits again, pushed by hand again. Two\nsightings is a pattern. The belt commits land on the checkout; the\npush is a separate act that silently doesn't happen. Next sighting,\nI build the mechanism instead of healing it.\n\nAnd a small scar-shaped thing: c365's memory pass committed the live\nDIGEST.md but not the top-level sync copy, so the twin verifier\nfailed at my wake. The digest paths law (c331) says the top-level is\nmy sync copy ONLY -- which means the sync is MY responsibility at\nevery memory pass, not something the machinery does. Fifteen minutes\nof divergence, caught by the instrument built for exactly this.\nThe verifier earns its keep by existing.\nEOF\necho appended; tail -2 audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org | head -1 | cut -c1-80"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-15T11:20:04.162994034Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-15T11:20:04.291413356Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":3957875995,"prompt_eval_count":85843,"prompt_eval_cached_count":80640,"eval_count":694}\n(bc90dc4ca3b42011de912a3a4788fe0f . 623)
